the holidays on Thanksgiving Americans  gather to break bread and share what  they're grateful for well what should  you do if you don't feel thankful maybe  your boss is a jerk maybe money's tight  maybe you're dreading awkward political  arguments with your relatives  whatever the reason you're not feeling  the holiday spirit so what are you  supposed to do three words act grateful  anyway  social science shows that choosing to  practice gratitude no matter how you  feel can itself make you more grateful  and happier too one 2003 study found  that people who kept a list of things  they were grateful for were  significantly more satisfied with their  lives than subjects who dwell on  negative or even neutral events instead  and thankfulness is contagious a 2011  study found that responding to an angry  person with warmth and gratitude disarms  their aggression and leads to better  behavior so here's the prescription for  the holiday blues forget about your  feelings and decide to count your  blessings it'll make you a happier  person and it'll probably make your  dinner companions happier too what do  you think about the research on  gratitude let us know in the comments  also let us know what other topics you'd  like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds  and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for  more research and videos from AEI
 

